{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:cb8b3d6ea54ee44d","name":"Blockade Runner","source":{"id":"source:reference-cb8b3d6ea54ee44d","title":"Blockade Runner","revision":16298,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:56:37Z","sha256":"7e73ff383295abe1319d7ccce555b178412f067c51977e91356fd2ac51c035c3","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=16298","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Blockade%20Runner&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-cb8b3d6ea54ee44d","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Space battles don't necessarily end when one side manages to disable the enemy's ship. instead, one might hear the sounds of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Docking Clamps"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Docking_Clamps","referenceId":"reference:b4a9e9f91fcb2a40"}," and breaching charges that signal the beginning of the next stage- the boarding action. Characters experienced in boarding actions might be Blockade Runners, brave souls who pilot ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"}," through enemy lines to bring news or supplies or to get word out of a desperate situation. They might be ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pirates"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pirates"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Privateers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Privateers"},", two words that both refer to someone hoping to take a ship, or at least it's cargo, intact. Some do it for profit, others to bolster a political cause, but all train to disable a ship and then prepare to fight those within to secure it.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Regardless of their motives or tactics, all Blockade Runners have a few traits in common. Most importantly, they plan to see combat on the inside of a ship they want in good condition, be it their own (if they expect to be boarded) or a prize ship they want to capture and sell or use to expand a private fleet. As a result, they focus on three details: convincing others foes to surrender; using the smallest, most precise blaster they can trust to complete the job; and learning to use melee weapons for close-quarters fighting around a Hyperdrive or concussion missile magazine.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Convincing a crew that they're better off surrendering than fighting takes a bold personality. Though they might have ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldiers"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ace Pilots"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ace_Pilots"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Elite Troopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Elite_Troopers"}," working with them, the best shipjackers are flamboyant, larger-than-life figures able to make outrageous claims and threats believably. As a result, they don't work well together; even when serving a larger cause, they prefer to operate in separate units.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Blockade Runner Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," 7/",{"tag":"a","children":["Master Privateer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Master_Privateer","referenceId":"reference:3791e7b9699989c6"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 5; ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"},":"]}," 2, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lure of Piracy"],"href":"https://sws